  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "If $A={-1,1}$ and $B={u,v},$ which of the following elements belong to $B\\times B\\times A?$\n\n- $(v,v,1)$\n- $((v,v),1)$\n- $(1,v,u)$",
  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B\\times C$ consists of all ordered triples whose first coordinate belongs to $A,$ second coordinate belongs to $B,$ and third coordinate belongs to $C.$\n\nIn this case, $B\\times B\\times A$ consists of every combination of ${u,v}$ with ${u,v}$ and ${-1,1},$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\\times B\\times A={ & (u,u,-1),(u,u,1),(u,v,-1),(u,v,1), \\\\  & (v,u,-1),(v,u,1),(v,v,-1),(v,v,1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n|B\\times B\\times A|=|B|\\cdot |B|\\cdot |A|=2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that only $(v,v,1)\\in B\\times B\\times A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
